    {
      "abstract": "The mid-central $P_{\\rm H}$ measurements reported in this work are shown alongside previous measurements in the upper panel, and are consistent with previous measurements at the energies studied here. The difference between integrated $P_{\\bar{\\Lambda}}$ and $P_{\\Lambda}$ is shown at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm{NN}}}$=19.6 and 27 GeV alongside previous measurements in the lower panel. The splittings observed with these high-statistics data sets are consistent with zero. Statistical uncertainties are represented as lines while systematic uncertainties are represented as boxes. The previous $P_{\\bar{\\Lambda}}-P_{\\Lambda}$ result at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}=7.7$ GeV is outside the axis range, but is consistent with zero within $2\\sigma$.",
